# 1. Review output - every report and archive under reviews/ is generated per run.
reviews/

# 2. Working intent files at the root. The intent agent renames the live document to
#    intent-YYYY-MM-DD-<n>.md on each new iteration, so both the live file and its
#    archives are noise in history. Only the fixture is source and must stay tracked.
/intent*.md
!/intent_example.md

# 3. Same for the spec chain: spec.md and spec-YYYY-MM-DD-<n>.md are working copies.
/spec*.md
#    /spec*.md only matches the root; a stray spec-YYYY-MM-DD.issues-Iteration_*.md copied into a
#    subfolder is the same noise, so the rule is repeated unanchored.
spec-*.md
!/spec_example.md

# 4. Local page-by-page dump of a PDF (bypage.csv). The review reads /report.csv, which is the
#    additional technical data; this is a working extract of how that file was produced.
/bypage.csv

# 5. .vscode/ is a local IDE configuration folder, not part of the kit.
.vscode/

# Runtime and macOS noise - a 13 MB .venv and TCC metadata are not part of the kit.
.venv/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
